<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">NOTES:  n  n1. The Company elected to exercise the option permitted under Section 115BAA of the Income Tax Act,  n1961 as introduced by the Taxation Laws (Amendment) Ordinance, 2019. Accordingly, the Company  nhas recognized Provision for Income Tax for the year ended 31 March 2020 and remeasured its  ndeferred tax assets and deferred tax liabilities basis the rate prescribed in the said section. The full  nimpact of this change has been recognized in the Statement of Profit and Loss.  n  n2. During the year, the Company divested rights and interests in two brands for a consideration of  nRs 37 crore. The income of Rs 31 crore (31 March 2019: Rs 29 crore), net of related expenses and  ndeferment of revenue as per Ind AS 115 on account of supply arrangement, is included in  n‘Other Income’.  n  n3. The Board of Directors at its Meeting held on 27 April 2020 declared a special (interim) dividend of  nRs 320 per equity share of Rs 10 each (3200%) for the financial year ended 31 March 2020. This being  nan event after the reporting date, in accordance with Ind AS 10, no adjustments have been made in  nthe financial statements for the year ended 31 March 2020.  n  nIn addition to the above, the Board of Directors had further at its Meeting held today, recommended  na final dividend of Rs 10 per equity share of Rs 10 each (100%) for the financial year ended 31 March  n2020.  n  n4. COVID-19, a pandemic caused by the novel Coronavirus, has emerged as an unprecedented  nchallenge globally and to the pharmaceutical companies in particular, who have a responsibility  ntowards public health. As a participant in this eco-system, the Company has taken a number of steps  nto respond to this unique situation. The Company has taken effective steps to ensure supply of  nessential medicines to its customers. The Company’s Goa Plant continues to remain operational at  nalmost its usual capacity. The Company has strictly followed the protocols on social distancing and  nprovided safe working environment at its Goa Plant.  n  nThe Company transitioned into a full Work From Home model and several measures were put in  nplace for communications, technology and productivity improvements to help employees cope with  nthis change. The Company also made various contributions to Government, health department,  npublic healthcare workers, etc., as part of its COVID-19 CSR initiatives.  nThere has been no significant adverse operational impact on the Company’s supply chain during  nMarch 2020 due to the Nationwide lockdown imposed by the Government of India in view of  nCOVID-19, a pandemic caused by the Novel Coronavirus. The Company has monitored the impact of  nCOVID-19 on all aspects of its business. The management has exercised due care, in concluding on  nsignificant accounting judgements and estimates, recoverability of receivables, assessment for  nimpairment of goodwill, intangible assets, inventory based on the information available as on date,  nwhile preparing the financial results as of and for the year ended 31 March 2020.  n  nIn view of the continued uncertainties and its inability to predict the extend and duration of  nCOVID-19 situation, the Company currently is unable to predict any future impact on its business  noperations. The Company will continue to ensure supply of essential medicines and take steps to  nmitigate any risks associated with COVID-19 pandemic.  n  n5. The current tax for quarter and year ended March 31, 2020 includes reversal of Rs. 44.5 Crore pertaining to prior years’ income tax provisions.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
